{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-16201" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=7\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhat are the ranges of $x$ and $y?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055537/state.json" "file_sha256" "4327eb4496c527ad13ff882fcb6a6f1dbd6cf80f251bbf1c60d11ab4257da82a"} {"question" "q-16201" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,$ we have $-1\\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ -7 & \\le 7\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 7 \\\\ -7 & \\le x\\le 7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $-7\\le x\\le 7.$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,$ we have $-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ -3 & \\le 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 3 \\\\ -3 & \\le y\\le 3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $-3\\le y\\le 3.$\n\nTherefore, the ranges are $-7\\le x\\le 7$ and $-3\\le y\\le 3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055537/state.json" "file_sha256" "4327eb4496c527ad13ff882fcb6a6f1dbd6cf80f251bbf1c60d11ab4257da82a"} {"question" "q-16201" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055537/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9f497ca129fe4bf8685b22d6f9988e14863b69109af99567731e9124323fc418"} {"question" "q-16201" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055537/state.json" "file_sha256" "4327eb4496c527ad13ff882fcb6a6f1dbd6cf80f251bbf1c60d11ab4257da82a"} {"question" "q-16201" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-3\\le x\\le 3,\\,-7\\le y\\le 7"] ["math" "-7\\le x\\le 7,\\,-3\\le y\\le 3"] ["math" "0\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le 7"] ["math" "0\\le x\\le 7,\\,0\\le y\\le 3"] ["math" "1\\le x\\le 1,\\,1\\le y\\le 1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055537/state.json" "file_sha256" "4327eb4496c527ad13ff882fcb6a6f1dbd6cf80f251bbf1c60d11ab4257da82a"} {"question" "q-16201" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-7\\le x\\le 7,\\,-3\\le y\\le 3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055537/state.json" "file_sha256" "4327eb4496c527ad13ff882fcb6a6f1dbd6cf80f251bbf1c60d11ab4257da82a"} {"question" "q-73602" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the graph of the following parametrically defined curve:\n\n$$\nx=2t-1,\\,\\,\\,y=2-{t}^{2},\\,-3\\le t\\le 3.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055537/state.json" "file_sha256" "4327eb4496c527ad13ff882fcb6a6f1dbd6cf80f251bbf1c60d11ab4257da82a"} {"question" "q-73602" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to create a table of values and then sketch the curve. First, we work out the $x$-values using the formula $x=2t-1.$ This gives\n\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-7$ | $-5$ | $-3$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $3$ | $5$ |\n| $y$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nNow, we work out the $y$ values using $y=2-{t}^{2}.$ This gives\n\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-7$ | $-5$ | $-3$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $3$ | $5$ |\n| $y$ | $-7$ | $-2$ | $1$ | $2$ | $1$ | $-2$ | $-7$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nPlotting these points, we obtain the following curve:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055537/assets/5cd074670c05cea0c68db75c7e1a57309c017c97556e976f2db4c3bf1b358a85.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055537/state.json" "file_sha256" "4327eb4496c527ad13ff882fcb6a6f1dbd6cf80f251bbf1c60d11ab4257da82a"} {"question" "q-73602" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055537/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9f497ca129fe4bf8685b22d6f9988e14863b69109af99567731e9124323fc418"} {"question" "q-73602" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055537/state.json" "file_sha256" "4327eb4496c527ad13ff882fcb6a6f1dbd6cf80f251bbf1c60d11ab4257da82a"} {"question" "q-73602" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055537/assets/0e7f02989d53152d1f2d5247f7f42d579956e49743694229d409cd266ec33e46.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055537/assets/1a7c98897aa0c13daff168b3804ac292c7662ee21f313ddd9e631019bcfbb814.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055537/assets/89b88f56878aeb33afe775e083c3775aaa701b6d293ca62e0bd3f2a78923159a.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055537/assets/9c8ed7ce4ee431e67b923ce3028819eb9f6f6b0a52cb892c93e582c31ba9d8af.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055537/assets/d06dfa9b8f6e87944014aa3eb03b6f83bd43e90624ba84d5d93d1d7f4e3beea6.png"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055537/state.json" "file_sha256" "4327eb4496c527ad13ff882fcb6a6f1dbd6cf80f251bbf1c60d11ab4257da82a"} {"question" "q-73602" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055537/assets/0e7f02989d53152d1f2d5247f7f42d579956e49743694229d409cd266ec33e46.png"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055537/state.json" "file_sha256" "4327eb4496c527ad13ff882fcb6a6f1dbd6cf80f251bbf1c60d11ab4257da82a"} {"question" "q-73623" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{t-2}+1,\\,\\,\\,y={t}^{3}+2,\\,t\\ge 2,\n$$\n\nwhat are the ranges of $x$ and $y?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055537/state.json" "file_sha256" "4327eb4496c527ad13ff882fcb6a6f1dbd6cf80f251bbf1c60d11ab4257da82a"} {"question" "q-73623" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ note that $\\sqrt{t-2}\\ge 0$ for all $t\\ge 2.$ Consequently, $x=\\sqrt{t-2}+1\\ge 1.$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ note that ${t}^{3}\\ge 8$ for all $t\\ge 2.$ Consequently, $y={t}^{3}+2\\ge 8+2=10.$\n\nTherefore, the ranges are $x\\ge 1$ and $y\\ge 10.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055537/state.json" "file_sha256" "4327eb4496c527ad13ff882fcb6a6f1dbd6cf80f251bbf1c60d11ab4257da82a"} {"question" "q-73623" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055537/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9f497ca129fe4bf8685b22d6f9988e14863b69109af99567731e9124323fc418"} {"question" "q-73623" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055537/state.json" "file_sha256" "4327eb4496c527ad13ff882fcb6a6f1dbd6cf80f251bbf1c60d11ab4257da82a"} {"question" "q-73623" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x\\ge -1,\\,y\\ge -2"] ["math" "x\\ge 1,\\,y\\ge 10"] ["math" "x\\ge 1,\\,y\\le 10"] ["math" "x\\le -1,\\,y\\ge -2"] ["math" "x\\le 1,\\,y\\le 10"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055537/state.json" "file_sha256" "4327eb4496c527ad13ff882fcb6a6f1dbd6cf80f251bbf1c60d11ab4257da82a"} {"question" "q-73623" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x\\ge 1,\\,y\\ge 10"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055537/state.json" "file_sha256" "4327eb4496c527ad13ff882fcb6a6f1dbd6cf80f251bbf1c60d11ab4257da82a"} {"question" "q-123785" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the graph of the following parametrically defined curve:\n\n$$\nx=5-{t}^{2},\\,y={t}^{2}-3,\\,0\\le t\\le 3\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055537/state.json" "file_sha256" "4327eb4496c527ad13ff882fcb6a6f1dbd6cf80f251bbf1c60d11ab4257da82a"} {"question" "q-123785" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to create a table of values and then sketch the curve. First, we work out the $x$-values using the formula $x=5-{t}^{2}.$ This gives\n\n| **$t$** | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $5$ | $4$ | $1$ | $-4$ |\n| $y$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nNow, we work out the $y$ values using $y={t}^{2}-3.$ This gives\n\n| **$t$** | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $5$ | $4$ | $1$ | $-4$ |\n| $y$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $1$ | $6$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nPlotting these points, we obtain the following curve:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055537/assets/a39e8a0c4ed269e5cb73aaedf0655d85302f3a5c3c7e91d9f5e58ebf84a82423.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055537/state.json" "file_sha256" "4327eb4496c527ad13ff882fcb6a6f1dbd6cf80f251bbf1c60d11ab4257da82a"} {"question" "q-123785" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055537/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9f497ca129fe4bf8685b22d6f9988e14863b69109af99567731e9124323fc418"} {"question" "q-123785" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055537/state.json" "file_sha256" "4327eb4496c527ad13ff882fcb6a6f1dbd6cf80f251bbf1c60d11ab4257da82a"} {"question" "q-123785" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055537/assets/06e9f6dca9a52ea97101e691426a98bf9c3fff46226b613f51948a0b6d5c21d8.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055537/assets/07a91c29e0b24b90570e1a656d8823a1ea3427863ec1e7e7ed80543869b